FE negative control — guest customer refuses when guest checkout is off.

Target spec:  app/components/auth/__tests__/auth-guest-customer.spec.ts
Behaviour:    "guest customer is disabled with a reason when guest checkout is
              off" — with the brand's GUEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED config false, the
              guest-customer entry must draw a stated disabled reason instead of
              starting a registration. Anchored to the behaviour, NOT to a
              line/case title: this spec is being re-based by a prover right
              now, so its case title and selectors may move under it.
Mutation:     replaces AuthGuestCustomer.vue's `guestCheckoutEnabled` guard —
              `!!getConfigValue(GUEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED)` — with a constant
              `true`, so the guard is gone and the entry is never disabled.
              (The GUEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED read lives in AuthGuestCustomer.vue,
              the component this spec mounts — not in the auth.vue page — so the
              hunk lands there.)
Why RED:      the spec mocks getConfigValue to return false and asserts the
              rendered text carries the disabled reason. With the guard forced
              true, the `v-if="!guestCheckoutEnabled"` disabled Alert never
              renders, so the disabled-reason assertion fails.
